    "result_text": "Everything is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and its GOLD test passes alongside `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier rule following the codebase's existing pattern for derived, create-time counts (`namesakeCount`), keeping each piece of logic in its own single-responsibility unit:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** `CountHousehold.java` \u2014 counts the new owner plus every existing owner sharing the same household identity (reusing `HouseholdNormalizer.key`, the same membership definition `AssignHousehold`/`EnsureUniqueHousehold` use) and stamps the built `Owner`. Mirrors `CountNamesakes`; runs before `SaveOwner` so it counts the not-yet-persisted new owner explicitly (`+1`).\n\n2. **Wired it** into `owners.POST.yml` between `assignHousehold` and `countNamesakes`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column), added to all four DB schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 added a GOLD branch that wins when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply unchanged. Tier stays computed in the one place it already lived (the mapper, at read/response time).\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (so the generated `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.GOLD` constant exists) and updated its description.\n\nThe GOLD check precedes the SILVER/BRONZE logic, so it correctly applies even though the test's household members have no email (which would otherwise make them BRONZE).",
